  "tabs": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "nodeId": "1328:1001",
      "sections": [
        {
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "A checkbox is a square control that users select or clear — used on its own, as a labeled field, or as a titled group of fields."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Overview",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Checkbox is built as three layered components, from atom to organism. Use the one that matches what you need: the bare control, a control with its label and messages, or a titled group of fields."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Components",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "CheckboxControl",
            "CheckboxField",
            "The box alone — border, fill, focus ring and check or dash icon. No label.",
            "Label, control, value text, and optional description, helper and error or warning messages.",
            "CheckboxGroup",
            "A group label with three CheckboxFields, vertical or horizontal."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Selection types",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Unselected",
            "Selected",
            "Indeterminate",
            "Not chosen.",
            "Chosen — shows a check.",
            "Mixed — shows a dash; exposed as aria-checked=\"mixed\"."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Formatting",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "Anatomy",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "1",
            "2",
            "3",
            "4",
            "5",
            "6",
            "•   ① Label — the field label (Has label).",
            "•   ② Description (optional) — text below the label (Has description).",
            "•   ③ Control — a CheckboxControl instance: box, border, focus ring, check or dash icon.",
            "•   ④ Value — the checkbox's own text, describing what checking it means (Value).",
            "•   ⑤ Error or warning message — icon and text, shown in the Invalid and Warning states.",
            "•   ⑥ Helper text (optional) — supporting text below the field (Has helper)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Sizes",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Small · 16px",
            "Medium · 20px",
            "Large · 24px",
            "Sizes apply to CheckboxControl. Shown at 2× for legibility."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Alignment",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Horizontal",
            "Fields sit side by side in one row.",
            "Vertical (default)",
            "Fields stack under the group label."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Content",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "Main elements",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Label",
            "•   The field or group title, set with the Label text property.",
            "Value",
            "•   The checkbox's own text, set with the Value text property — describes what checking it means.",
            "Description and helper text",
            "•   Optional supporting text — description sits under the label, helper text under the field.",
            "Error and warning messages",
            "•   Shown as text with a status icon in the Invalid and Warning states, so validation never relies on color alone."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Overflow content",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Label and value text wrap. The skill defines a truncate-text option (ellipsis instead of wrapping); it isn't exposed as a Figma property yet."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Behaviors",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": []
        },
        {
          "heading": "States",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Each field has a selection type — Unselected, Selected or Indeterminate — and a field state. Field states map to the control's type and state; for example, Invalid switches the control to its Error type.",
            "•   Enabled — resting.",
            "•   Focus — keyboard focus; the control shows a 3px focus ring (border/interactive/focus).",
            "•   Invalid — error border and an error message.",
            "•   Warning — a warning message.",
            "•   Read-only — value text is dimmed and the value can't be changed.",
            "•   Disabled — label, value and box are dimmed; the field is non-interactive.",
            "•   Skeleton — placeholder shapes while content loads.",
            "CheckboxControl adds Hovered and Pressed pointer states. See the Style tab for how each state looks."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Interactions",
          "level": 4,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Keyboard",
            "Key",
            "Action",
            "Tab",
            "Moves focus to the next checkbox",
            "Shift",
            "+",
            "Tab",
            "Moves focus to the previous checkbox",
            "Disabled checkboxes don't receive keyboard focus. Full keyboard details are on the Accessibility tab."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Related",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Checkbox is reused inside other components in this system.",
            "•   List item — uses CheckboxControl as its leading or trailing control for multi-select lists."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
