    {
      "title": "Accessibility",
      "nodeId": "1328:2585",
      "sections": [
        {
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "A checkbox is a square control that users select or clear — used on its own, as a labeled field, or as a titled group of fields."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "What the design system provides",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "•   A Focus state with a 3px ring outside the box, on every type.",
            "•   An Indeterminate type for mixed selection.",
            "•   Error and warning messages as text with an icon, not color alone.",
            "•   Disabled and Read-only states for the field."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Development considerations",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "•   Use role=\"checkbox\" (or a native checkbox) with aria-checked — \"mixed\" for Indeterminate.",
            "•   Group related checkboxes with role=\"group\", labelled by the group label.",
            "•   Set aria-invalid on fields in the Invalid state and associate the error message with the control.",
            "•   Disabled checkboxes must not receive keyboard focus.",
            "•   Make the value text part of the clickable area — the box alone is 16–24px."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Keyboard interactions",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Key",
            "Action",
            "Tab",
            "Moves focus to the next checkbox",
            "Shift",
            "+",
            "Tab",
            "Moves focus to the previous checkbox"
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Design recommendations",
          "level": 3,
          "paragraphs": [
            "Automated contrast check — WCAG 2.x relative luminance (sRGB), against the page surface (surface/bg/default) or the box fill, for every theme combination. Minimums: 3:1 for the box, border and focus ring (non-text UI), 4.5:1 for text, 3:1 for disabled text (house rule TKN-005). Note: project-a / light is measured against the current surface/bg/default, which resolves to blue because of the gray/50 token."
          ]
        },
